Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: libtiff/tif_pixarlog.c
Line: 179
Function: horizontalAccumulateF
Bug type: out-of-bounds-write
CWE: CWE-787
Explanation: If stride is 0 (e.g., due to an invalid SamplesPerPixel), the REPEAT macro (defined at lines 109–118) executes its body once even when asked to repeat 0 times. In the else-branch starting at line 177, REPEAT(stride, ...) runs once, then n -= stride leaves n unchanged, and the subsequent while (n > 0) loop never terminates. The body increments wp and op and dereferences them on each iteration, causing unbounded out-of-bounds reads/writes.

Source context:
```c
